IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text):
-- section 199 (Part 6, Division 1): accounting records and systems of control. ss 200 and 200A are shown repealed (see NOTES.md, coverage).
--
-- Reading a result (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words
-- (a duty not met, which is the provision's own question; a flat negative; a closed gate); NOTHING is "not covered" (the text is silent,
-- limits its grant in its own wording and the case falls outside, or points outside the sources). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every name begins with the label of the provision it implements, so that no other part can define the same name.
-- Whether a company is "public", or a "subsidiary company" of a public company, is decided elsewhere (s 4(1); s 209A, another part's):
-- the answer is taken as an input named for the fact.

§ `Section 199: the acts of the regulative rules of this section`

-- The acts the regulative rules below are about. The party is a company (core: Company), a type the core already declares.
DECLARE `s 199 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 199(1) cause accounting and other records to be kept`
    `s 199(2) dispose of the records within 5 years from the end of the financial year in which the transactions or operations are completed`
    `s 199(2A) devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls`
    `s 199(3) keep the records open to inspection by the directors`

§ `Section 199(1): the records a company must cause to be kept`

-- src:17857 | Accounting records and systems of control
-- src:17859 | 199.—(1) Every company must cause to be kept such accounting
-- src:17860 | and other records as will sufficiently explain the transactions and
-- src:17861 | financial position of the company and enable true and fair financial
-- src:17862 | statements and any documents required to be attached thereto to be
-- src:17863 | prepared from time to time, and must cause those records to be kept in
-- src:17864 | such manner as to enable them to be conveniently and properly
-- src:17865 | audited.
@ref s 199(1) (src:17857-17865)
GIVEN `the records sufficiently explain the transactions and financial position of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records enable true and fair financial statements and any documents required to be attached to them to be prepared from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records are kept in such manner as to enable them to be conveniently and properly audited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(1) the company has caused the records to be kept as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the records sufficiently explain the transactions and financial position of the company`
       AND `the records enable true and fair financial statements and any documents required to be attached to them to be prepared from time to time`
       AND `the records are kept in such manner as to enable them to be conveniently and properly audited`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must cause to be kept such accounting and other records as will sufficiently explain the transactions and financial position of the company" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the party is the company; the text gives no time limit and no consequence inside the subsection
-- (the consequence is the offence in subsection (6)), so no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 199(1) (src:17859-17865)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 199 act`
`s 199(1) a company must cause accounting and other records to be kept` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 199(1) cause accounting and other records to be kept`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not cause accounting and other records to be kept"

§ `Section 199(2): how long the records must be retained`

-- src:17869 | (2) The company must retain the records referred to in
-- src:17870 | subsection (1) for a period of not less than 5 years from the end of
-- src:17871 | the financial year in which the transactions or operations to which
-- src:17872 | those records relate are completed.
@ref s 199(2) (src:17869-17872)
GIVEN `the last day of the financial year in which the transactions or operations to which the records relate are completed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 199(2) the last day of the period for which the company must retain the records` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the last day of the financial year in which the transactions or operations to which the records relate are completed` 5 Years

@ref s 199(2) (src:17869-17872)
GIVEN `the last day of the financial year in which the transactions or operations to which the records relate are completed` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(2) the subsection requires the company to retain the records on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day asked about` AT MOST `the last day of the financial year in which the transactions or operations to which the records relate are completed`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period runs "from the end of the financial year in which the transactions or operations ... are completed", so a day on or before that end is outside it, and subsection (1) is what applies then
    ELSE IF `the day asked about` AT MOST `s 199(2) the last day of the period for which the company must retain the records` `the last day of the financial year in which the transactions or operations to which the records relate are completed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not less than 5 years from the end of the financial year" (a period the text fixes in its own words; after it the subsection requires nothing: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- "must retain ... for a period of not less than 5 years from the end of the financial year" is read as a prohibition on disposing of the records
-- inside the 5 years (SHANT, with the period as the clock): the same duty seen from the act that breaches it. The clock counts days from the end of the financial year.
@ref s 199(2) (src:17869-17872)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days in the 5 years from the end of the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 199 act`
`s 199(2) a company must not dispose of the records within 5 years from the end of the financial year` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 199(2) dispose of the records within 5 years from the end of the financial year in which the transactions or operations are completed`
    WITHIN `the number of days in the 5 years from the end of the financial year`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company disposed of the records before the end of the 5 years from the end of the financial year in which the transactions or operations were completed"

§ `Section 199(2A): the system of internal accounting controls`

-- src:17876 | (2A) Every public company and every subsidiary company of a
-- src:17877 | public company must devise and maintain a system of internal
-- src:17878 | accounting controls sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance
-- src:17879 | that —
-- src:17881 | (a) assets are safeguarded against loss from unauthorised use
-- src:17882 | or disposition; and
-- src:17884 | (b) transactions are properly authorised and that they are
-- src:17885 | recorded as necessary to permit the preparation of true and
-- src:17886 | fair financial statements and to maintain accountability of
-- src:17887 | assets.
@ref s 199(2A) (src:17876-17887)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a subsidiary company of a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(2A) the company must devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` OR `the company is a subsidiary company of a public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every public company and every subsidiary company of a public company must devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls" names these companies and says nothing of any other (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

@ref s 199(2A) (src:17876-17887)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a subsidiary company of a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has devised and maintains a system of internal accounting controls` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that assets are safeguarded against loss from unauthorised use or disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that transactions are properly authorised and recorded as necessary to permit the preparation of true and fair financial statements and to maintain accountability of assets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(2A) the company has devised and maintained the system the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is a public company` OR `the company is a subsidiary company of a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid on "every public company and every subsidiary company of a public company" and the subsection is silent on any other company
    ELSE IF    `the company has devised and maintains a system of internal accounting controls`
            AND `the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that assets are safeguarded against loss from unauthorised use or disposition`
            AND `the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that transactions are properly authorised and recorded as necessary to permit the preparation of true and fair financial statements and to maintain accountability of assets`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that — (a) assets are safeguarded ...; and (b) transactions are properly authorised" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

@ref s 199(2A) (src:17876-17887)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 199 act`
`s 199(2A) a public company or a subsidiary company of a public company must devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 199(2A) devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls"

§ `Section 199(3): where the records are kept, and the directors' access`

-- src:17891 | (3) The records referred to in subsection (1) must be kept at the
-- src:17892 | registered office of the company or at such other place as the directors
-- src:17893 | think fit and must at all times be open to inspection by the directors.
@ref s 199(3) (src:17891-17893)
GIVEN `the records are kept at the registered office of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records are kept at another place that the directors think fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records are at all times open to inspection by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(3) the records are kept as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    (`the records are kept at the registered office of the company` OR `the records are kept at another place that the directors think fit`)
       AND `the records are at all times open to inspection by the directors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The records referred to in subsection (1) must be kept at the registered office of the company or at such other place as the directors think fit and must at all times be open to inspection by the directors" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

@ref s 199(3) (src:17891-17893)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(3) the records must be open to inspection by the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says the records must be open to inspection "by the directors" and is silent on anyone else

@ref s 199(3) (src:17891-17893)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 199 act`
`s 199(3) a company must keep its accounting records open to inspection by the directors` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 199(3) keep the records open to inspection by the directors`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not keep its accounting records open to inspection by the directors"

§ `Section 199(4): records kept outside Singapore`

-- src:17898 | (4) If accounting and other records are kept by the company at a
-- src:17899 | place outside Singapore there must be sent to and kept at a place in
-- src:17900 | Singapore and be at all times open to inspection by the directors such
-- src:17901 | statements and returns with respect to the business dealt with in the
-- src:17902 | records so kept as will enable to be prepared true and fair financial
-- src:17903 | statements and any documents required to be attached thereto.
@ref s 199(4) (src:17898-17903)
GIVEN `the accounting and other records are kept by the company at a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(4) the company must send to and keep at a place in Singapore statements and returns` MEANS
    IF `the accounting and other records are kept by the company at a place outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If accounting and other records are kept by the company at a place outside Singapore there must be sent to and kept at a place in Singapore ..." (a failed "if": marginal reading (a), NOTES.md)

@ref s 199(4) (src:17898-17903)
GIVEN `the accounting and other records are kept by the company at a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `statements and returns with respect to the business dealt with in the records so kept have been sent to and kept at a place in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those statements and returns are at all times open to inspection by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those statements and returns enable true and fair financial statements and any documents required to be attached to them to be prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(4) the company has complied with the subsection` MEANS
    IF NOT `the accounting and other records are kept by the company at a place outside Singapore`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of records "kept by the company at a place outside Singapore" and is silent on records kept in Singapore
    ELSE IF    `statements and returns with respect to the business dealt with in the records so kept have been sent to and kept at a place in Singapore`
            AND `those statements and returns are at all times open to inspection by the directors`
            AND `those statements and returns enable true and fair financial statements and any documents required to be attached to them to be prepared`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there must be sent to and kept at a place in Singapore and be at all times open to inspection by the directors such statements and returns ... as will enable to be prepared true and fair financial statements" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

§ `Section 199(5): the Court's order for inspection by a public accountant acting for a director`

-- src:17907 | (5) The Court may in any particular case order that the accounting
-- src:17908 | and other records of a company be open to inspection by a public
-- src:17909 | accountant acting for a director, but only upon an undertaking in
-- src:17910 | writing given to the Court that information acquired by the public
-- src:17911 | accountant during his or her inspection must not be disclosed by the
-- src:17912 | public accountant except to that director.
@ref s 199(5) (src:17907-17912)
GIVEN `the public accountant is acting for a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an undertaking in writing has been given to the Court that information acquired by the public accountant during the inspection must not be disclosed by the public accountant except to that director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(5) the Court may order the records to be open to inspection by the public accountant` MEANS
    IF NOT `the public accountant is acting for a director of the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a public accountant acting for a director" and is silent on anyone else
    ELSE IF `an undertaking in writing has been given to the Court that information acquired by the public accountant during the inspection must not be disclosed by the public accountant except to that director`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only upon an undertaking in writing given to the Court that information acquired by the public accountant during his or her inspection must not be disclosed by the public accountant except to that director" (a gate the text closes with "only")

§ `Section 199(6): the offence of default and its penalty`

-- What the court may impose on conviction. "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months and also to a default penalty":
-- a fine OR imprisonment (not both: the text says "or"), and a default penalty in addition. The default penalty's amount is s 408's (not among the sources).
DECLARE `s 199(6) penalty` HAS
    `s 199(6) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 199(6) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 199(6) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 199(6) a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:17914 | (6) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:17915 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:17916 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:17917 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months and
-- src:17918 | also to a default penalty.
@ref s 199(6) (src:17914-17918)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 199` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 199` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of the offence: the provision's own question; fork F-S1 of NOTES.md)

@ref s 199(6) (src:17914-17918)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 199` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 199(6) penalty`
`s 199(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 199(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 199` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 199(6) penalty` OF 10000, 12, FALSE, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of "the offence" the subsection creates; where the person is not guilty of it the subsection fixes no penalty
